description:
About Us
Welcome to Barry Nilsson. For 60 years, we’ve been shaping a better experience for our clients and our people. What sets our firm apart is not just what we do, but who we are: a team known for its collaborative spirit and commitment to excellence, inclusion, and innovation. As an award-winning national law firm, we’ve built a culture that empowers you to not only grow your career, but be your authentic self while you do it.
About the Team
You will join a tight knit and collegiate Technology team comprising 9 people who provide IT support to the firm nationally. Reporting to the Head of IT, with a dotted line to the Business Projects and Transformation Manager, you will work in a fast-paced and service-focussed team. 
About the Role
We’re seeking an experienced Data Analyst to join our team. The role will maintain data storage, assess database design, and gather, organise, and interpret data and statistical information based on the data.  As well as servicing client reporting needs, the role will be key in providing insight which can be used to make business decisions and drive positive client outcomes.
Responsibilities of this role include:
providing information from existing data sources, using a variety of reporting tools for all company divisions;
providing standard and ad-hoc reporting, including key performance indicator (KPI) reporting, metrics definition and data collection to support KPIs; creation and maintenance of reports and Dashboards;
managing data to support reporting, including the creation and maintenance of databases, through the use of MS SQL Server, SSRS/SSIS;
analysing data and writing meaningful reports using SQL Server; and
designing and developing customised web dashboards for our practice management system, Aderant.
Please note that we are open to permanent or 12-month contract arrangements.
About you
We’re seeking someone with:
relevant tertiary qualifications;
experience as a Data Analyst, ideally in a law firm or professional services environment;
extensive experience developing reports with MS SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS), T-SQL, and other reporting tools, including a high level competency with SQL scripting;
hands on experience with SSIS, SSRS, and Power BI (including data modelling and DAX);
extensive experience designing and developing dashboards;
experience with Aderant or similar Legal PMS would be advantageous; and
experience with Clio ShareDo or similar Legal MMS would be advantageous.
Please note that we are open to candidates in Brisbane, Melbourne, Sydney, Perth, Adelaide or Hobart.
Benefits of Working with Us
Just to name a few, we have:
been acknowledged as an ‘Employer of Choice’ for the last 7 years;
a supportive environment where managers genuinely care about your wellbeing;
opportunities for structured mentorship and continuous professional development;
progressive policies including a 9.5-day fortnight, working from home, purchase of leave options, volunteer leave, and a public holiday swap policy;
an annual performance bonus scheme designed to recognise and reward strong performance;  
a relaxed office environment where you can “Dress for your Day”;
access to our Health & Wellbeing program, BNWell, which supports the mental, physical and financial wellbeing of our people including a yearly health & wellbeing allowance and a health & wellbeing leave day; and
a shared care parental policy with equal leave for all parents.
Ready to Go Further?
From your first day, expect to be embraced for who you are — because we’re a firm defined by our people. Step into a workplace where individuality is celebrated, ambitions are realised, and collaboration drives success. At Barry Nilsson, it’s about being you and going further. Apply today.
To make a confidential application, please click ‘Apply Now’ and address your application to Monika Geschke, People & Culture Adviser.
Barry Nilsson is committed to building a diverse, inclusive and flexible workplace where all of our people are supported to be their authentic selves, valued for their unique contributions, rewarded fairly, connected to colleagues, and empowered to achieve their full potential. We welcome applications from Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander peoples, LGBTIQ+, as well as people of all ages, genders, abilities and cultures. Feel free to chat to the recruiter for this position regarding any accommodations or adjustments you may require to the role or the recruitment process to ensure your equitable participation.

12 month contract
Python or R - AWS S3 - LLMs & Gen AI
ACT, NSW or VIC Address - Hybrid 3/2 dpw
Our client, a Commonwealth Government organisation whose focus is to provide support to Australian's living with disability, require the services of a AI Data Scientist.
Duties of the AI Data Scientist
Research & implement innovative techniques and interdisciplinary methods to solve business issues with a focus on application of AI/data science and statistical techniques;
Designing statistical, mathematical, & various data science models to conduct analytical work that addresses business issues, & development of new products;
Present outcomes of work undertaken, tailored to context & stakeholders;
Undertake ad hoc modelling & data science requests.
 Skills and Experience Required
4+ years of experience as a Data Scientist in either public or private sector;
Experience with complex internal or external stakeholder engagement & management;
Proficient Python or R programming skills including data manipulation, analysis & model development/deployment;
Demonstrated experience in application of Artificial Intelligence & Data Science techniques & processes;
A growth mindset & demonstrated initiative in exploring, learning, & applying new data science techniques & processes to improve DaSH capabilities & project outcomes;
Proficient in SQL, accessing databases & data storage systems (e.g AWS S3) (desired);
Working knowledge of Language Models, Large Language Models & Generative AI & how they can be used effectively (desired);
Working knowledge & understanding of AI Assurance & Governance frameworks relating to the development of ethically sound & safe AI systems (desired).
How to Apply 
For a copy of the full job description, including the application instructions, please get in touch with 
Ben at Recruitment Hive by clicking the Quick Apply button. Alternatively you can reach Ben on (02) 6299 1*** to discuss further. 
Please note that applications close on Friday the 6th of March 2026 at 11am. Recruitment Hive welcome late applications to be considered for future opportunities. 
Job ID: BC666224 | LH-05727
We Value Diversity 
The Recruitment Hive is a proud Equal Opportunity Employer. We recognise the value of diverse perspectives and experience and are committed to an inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and respected for who they are. We encourage people with disability, indigenous, veterans and people of all backgrounds and abilities to express their interest in this role.
